{"c":[{"id":"1928d54605e94465","sum":"Chrome web AX: nativeYields; publish invalidates offer. H14: pagetask start, no guest Jev, banners cover panels. Live sets once; HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS false. W1: guard-adversary class(a) writes 0; labelled lines offer parts; writeMisfit owns rules; candidates added, never swapped.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"686710946312e7ea","sum":"Chrome ignores native AX writes once web AX is on (HostCoordinator yields via PageInline.nativeYields); PageTaskMachine.publish invalidates its live offer first. H14 rig: no guest Jev, use 'pagetask start'; banners cover top-right panels.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"806a636804d6e5d8","sum":"Chrome page fields: once web AX is on, Chrome ignores native AX writes (HostCoordinator yields via PageInline.nativeYields); PageTaskMachine.publish invalidates its own live offer before republishing, or onDisplaced drops the page task.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T172603Z-a7ca0252d9058e55","text":"Once an assistive app turns on Chrome's web accessibility, native ghost text sees page fields, but Chrome ignores its AX writes (writeIgnored): Tab is eaten. HostCoordinator yields to page inline text via PageInline.nativeYields.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T211151Z-05df8b8f447e91f6","text":"H14: PageTaskMachine.publish must invalidate its own live offer before republishing (a click changes the preview without a key): otherwise the arbiter's onDisplaced puts the whole page task away.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cfa933fb97832a8e","sum":"H14 rig: guest has no Jev; drive attach rows with hook 'pagetask start <goalProgress>' (pageTask.lastAccept* shows Tab). Banners cover top-right panels: give canned page goals a lower viewport. clickableContent panels need a mouse move before a click.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T211204Z-63399dc84dfcee60","text":"H14: the rig guest has no Jev, so an Ask gives no page goal; drive attach rows with test hook 'pagetask start <goalProgress>'. The helper echoes no goalAccept: state pageTask.lastAccept* shows what Tab sent.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T211204Z-f2f5d457e6044752","text":"H14: macOS notification banners cover Caret's panels at the screen's top right; a rig click there hits the banner. Give canned page goals a viewport lower down. clickableContent panels take a click only after a mouse move over them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ca6b56f177286a70","sum":"Live Jev: run sets once (43-81 requests/pass); HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS false (LV1). W1: offline guard-adversary.ts each batch, class (a) writes 0; labelled lines offer parts. All chosen writes use fill/writable.ts writeMisfit; add rules there; candidates added, never swapped.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"99b0cde49d41360f","sum":"Live Jev: run live sets once (R1's slow-eval never settles; each pass sends 43-81 new requests). Keep HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS false: on, Jev answered 'none' on names and emails on four small forms (LV1 compare-hoist.txt).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T015102Z-70f8faec6a3a0648","text":"R1's slow-eval runner never settles on live Jev: each pass sends 43-81 new requests, so a set costs about 3x one pass. Run live sets once.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T015102Z-cf129cc10068e635","text":"HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS changes Jev's answers: with it on, Jev answered 'none' on names and emails on four small forms. Keep it false (LV1 compare-hoist.txt).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5678229122db2693","sum":"W1: run helper/scripts/guard-adversary.ts offline each batch; class (a) writes must stay 0. Labelled multi-value lines offer parts, not whole lines. All chosen-value writes use fill/writable.ts writeMisfit; add rules there. Candidates are added, never swapped.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T020955Z-5dafeedfea56fda2","text":"W1: canned evals never pick a plausible wrong candidate; run helper/scripts/guard-adversary.ts (offline, ~2 s) each batch: class (a) writes must stay 0. A labelled multi-value line offers its parts, not its whole (line-values severalValues).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T025421Z-86d442b2d62eead8","text":"Any path that writes a chosen value into a field checks fill/writable.ts writeMisfit (fill, planner validate, codeplan, offer filter, goal gate); add new value rules there, not beside one caller. Candidates are only added, never swapped out.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6c91d936f6921fcb","sum":"G2/W2/A2-I3: notes go whole before clauses; canned evals read web-form/owners.json; page writes need a CheckedValue (test/mint.ts). Ask scope is Jev's per-field ask, code only vetoes; reword -> ask-scope-eval.ts; $0 replays: CARET_JEV_CACHE_MODE=replay, nonzero --spend-limit.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f9ac8be3313a624c","sum":"G2: note lines go whole before clauses; contact clauses charge first outside chats; canned evals answer owners from owners.json. W2/I1: every page write needs a CheckedValue or compilers throw; test mints use test/mint.ts minted(p, model).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9eb8c86cfea56fc0","sum":"G2: note short lines go whole before clauses; date/email/phone partAround clauses charge first only outside chats (earlier, canned 316->308). Canned page-loop evals answer owners from fixtures/web-form/owners.json, else unclear 0.5; a page with no entry throws.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T034441Z-339e891dadd6a49a","text":"G2: a note's short lines go out whole and spend its budget before any clause; date/email/phone clause parts (partAround) are charged before other lines only outside conversations; earlier charging cut emails and names (guard-adversary canned 316 -> 308/314).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T034441Z-3d8738b69dcb6bd3","text":"G2: canned page-loop evals answer fill's ownership questions from fixtures/web-form/owners.json (W4: ~/.caret-run/evidence/browser/w4/replay/owners.json), unclear 0.5 elsewhere; a canned run throws for a page with no entry.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"eafc5c507969e166","sum":"W2/I1: every page write needs a CheckedValue (fill/contract.ts checkValues/mintExempt) or compilers throw ContractError; provenanceStale is the one source recheck and lines [] never holds, so hand-built test mints use test/mint.ts minted(p, model).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T050339Z-4d8696f9c3182cf8","text":"W2: every page write needs a CheckedValue from helper/src/fill/contract.ts (checkValues or mintExempt); compilers (fillPlan, validatePlan, GoalRuns.propose, patterns plan) throw ContractError without one. Proposals built by hand in tests go through test/mint.ts.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T091312Z-bde14560b8505461","text":"I1: the only source recheck is fill/contract.ts provenanceStale (G2's sourceHolds merged in, deleted); a window Provenance needs lines = lineDigests of the text Jev judged, and lines [] is never held, so hand-built test mints pass a model (test/mint.ts minted(p, model)).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e2dc524fd37e482b","sum":"A2-I3: Ask scope = Jev's per-field scope ask, code only vetoes (A2's reading rules failed); reword -> rerun ask-scope-eval.ts; $0 replays: CARET_JEV_CACHE_MODE=replay, no CARET_ENV_FILE, nonzero --spend-limit; resolver date guesses go to the verifier.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0ac61137cde78f4e","sum":"Ask scope is Jev's per-field scope ask (asks/not/unclear, 2 wordings, SCOPE_CUTOFF); code only vetoes, never hand-written reading rules (A2's 12 rounds failed). After rewording, recalibrate with scripts/ask-scope-eval.ts (--answers rescores free).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T094325Z-2ecfd9f27d40a67e","text":"Ask scope is Jev's per-field scope ask (asks/not/unclear, two wordings, SCOPE_CUTOFF); code only vetoes. Answer a widening finding with a veto or 'unclear', never a hand-written reading rule: A2's twelve rounds of those never converged.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T094325Z-46934d63d09e671d","text":"Recalibrate SCOPE_CUTOFF after changing the scope ask's wording: scripts/ask-scope-eval.ts scores Jev's answers against scripts/ask-scope-labels.json; --answers rescores a saved run for free.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b8239301d4a3ddf5","sum":"I2-I3: $0 Ask replays need CARET_JEV_CACHE_MODE=replay, no CARET_ENV_FILE and a nonzero --spend-limit; any resolver date assumption (reference year, format order, century) goes to the verifier with Provenance.says, never a raw span.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T103113Z-2eca6bf2c96e40c9","text":"Ask evals: realfill-asks --spend-limit 0 refuses replayed requests too; for a $0 replay set CARET_JEV_CACHE_MODE=replay, unset CARET_ENV_FILE and pass a nonzero --spend-limit (misses fail as jevFailed).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T113449Z-ded1f2a70adbf732","text":"fill dates: any resolver assumption (year from a reference, order from a format/locale, century) sends the value to the verifier with Provenance.says; send-line years and stated-format orders are offered as their own candidates; a raw span never takes them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
